  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Trade Centre  was founded in 1964 under the auspices of the WTO &amp; UNCTAD. It seeks to enable small business export success in developing countries, with priority accorded to women, youth and migrants. ITC works with trade support institutions so that they are better able to support exporters, especially women and youth led enterprises. Ireland is a member of ITC&apos;s Joint Advisory Group (JAG) which meets annually to examine the activities of ITC.</narrative>
